Source: honor-fmbp
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Philip Walsh <packages@drphilth.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), dh-dkms
Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: honor-fmbp-hwmon-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 (FMB-P) fan tachometer hwmon driver (DKMS)
 Reads the two fan speeds from EC RAM (reverse-engineered: LE16 words at
 0x2C/0x2E) and exposes them as a standard hwmon device, so `sensors` and
 desktop monitors show fan RPM. Read-only — fan control stays with the EC.
 DMI-gated: the module only binds on HONOR FMB-P hardware.

Package: honor-fmbp-kbdlight-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 (FMB-P) keyboard backlight driver (DKMS)
 Drives the keyboard backlight through the EC KBBL register (0x41) and
 exposes it as a standard ::kbd_backlight LED class device, giving GNOME
 (and upower) the usual backlight controls. Works independently of the
 DSDT fix. DMI-gated: the module only binds on HONOR FMB-P hardware.

Package: honor-fmbp-dsdt
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, initramfs-tools | dracut
Description: HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 (FMB-P) corrected ACPI DSDT (boot-critical)
 The FMB-P firmware DSDT aborts at load time (NFC0/GNUM), which hides the
 NVMe drive and breaks the touchpad; the same table also leaves the
 touchscreen unpowered. This package ships a corrected DSDT (OEM revision
 bumped so the kernel accepts it) and prepends it as an uncompressed early
 cpio (kernel/firmware/acpi/dsdt.aml, CONFIG_ACPI_TABLE_UPGRADE), re-applied
 automatically on every kernel and initramfs update. It supports whichever
 initramfs generator is already present — an initramfs-tools hook and a
 dracut acpi_override drop-in are both shipped, and only the active
 generator's mechanism fires — so it never forces a generator swap or a
 network fetch (important for the offline pre-first-boot install).
 .
 The FMB-P ships in two BIOS variants (global and Chinese) whose DSDTs differ
 in their NVS base addresses; both corrected tables are included and the right
 one is selected at install time by matching the live firmware DSDT's GNVS
 signature (honor-fmbp-dsdt-select). The Chinese variant is untested on real
 Chinese hardware — see README.Debian. On non-FMB-P machines nothing is applied.

Package: honor-fmbp-config
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, udev, dconf-cli
Recommends: pkexec
Description: HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 (FMB-P) input, device and power quirks
 Udev rules and hwdb entries for FMB-P input quirks:
  * inhibit the FTSC1000 touchscreen's bogus second HID collection, which
    spams KEY_MICMUTE (~30/s) while the panel is touched;
  * silence the meaningless EC scancode e078 sent alongside Fn hotkeys;
  * grant group `input` write access to the touchscreen's `inhibited`
    attribute, plus /usr/bin/honor-fmbp-touchscreen-toggle to flip it
    (pkexec fallback for users outside that group; --power for a true
    panel power toggle via the DSDT PowerResource).
 .
 Power quirks:
  * honor-battery-thresholds.service restores the EC charge-limit preset at
    boot (configurable via /etc/default/honor-fmbp-battery; the EC does not
    persist it across reboots);
  * a dconf default aligns the GNOME "Battery Health Charging" extension's
    Quick Settings presets with the ranges huawei-wmi actually enforces.

Package: honor-fmbp-archive-keyring
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 (FMB-P) PPA apt source and signing key
 Configures the ppa:drphilth/honor-fmbp apt repository as a file-based source:
 it installs the PPA's OpenPGP signing key to /usr/share/keyrings and a deb822
 .sources file that references it.
 .
 Installing this package "adds the PPA" without any network access — no
 add-apt-repository, no keyserver round-trip — so it can be applied from the
 installer chroot while offline. The repository itself is only contacted later,
 on apt update/upgrade, once the machine is booted with networking.

Package: honor-magicbook-pro-14
Architecture: all
Depends: honor-fmbp-hwmon-dkms (= ${source:Version}),
         honor-fmbp-kbdlight-dkms (= ${source:Version}),
         honor-fmbp-dsdt (= ${source:Version}),
         honor-fmbp-config (= ${source:Version}),
         honor-fmbp-archive-keyring (= ${source:Version}),
         firmware-sof-signed,
         libpam-fprintd,
         ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: honor-fmbp-libfprint-sdcp, gnome-shell-extension-manager
Description: HONOR MagicBook Pro 14 2025 (FMB-P) Ubuntu enablement (metapackage)
 Installs everything needed to run Ubuntu on the HONOR MagicBook Pro 14
 2025 (FMB-P): the corrected boot-critical DSDT, fan and keyboard
 backlight drivers, input quirks and fingerprint PAM integration, and
 pulls in the Intel SOF audio firmware (firmware-sof-signed, from the
 Ubuntu archive) that this machine's DSP audio needs. The SDCP
 fingerprint driver fork (honor-fmbp-libfprint-sdcp)
 is recommended and comes from the same PPA. gnome-shell-extension-manager
 is recommended for installing the battery-charge-limit Quick Settings panel
 (see honor-fmbp-config's README.Debian).
